[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a quick‑reference guide that shows **every practical way** to add a searchable address / place box to a map that is built with **Mapbox GL JS v2**.  
It is split into three sections:

| Section | What it covers |
|---------|----------------|
| 1️⃣  | The **official Mapbox‑provided** geocoder (the one most people start with). |
| 2️⃣  | **Open‑source / self‑hosted** alternatives that work with Mapbox GL JS (or with a future MapLibre migration). |
| 3️⃣  | **“Hybrid” / commercial** services you can call from the browser (e.g., HERE, Google, MapTiler) and plug into the same UI component. |

For each option I list:

* **Package / CDN** you need to import.  
* **How to wire it to a Mapbox GL JS v2 map** (code snippet).  
* **Key pros / cons** (license, cost, rate‑limits, UI features, ease of styling).  
* **Typical gotchas** (token handling, CORS, attribution, required CSS, etc.).

---

## 1️⃣ Official Mapbox Geocoder (Mapbox GL Geocoder)

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Package** | `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` (npm) or the CDN `https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js` (version numbers may change). |
| **CSS** | `https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css` |
| **Installation** | ```bash npm install @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder``` |
| **Basic usage** | ```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = '<YOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN>'; // required

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.44, 37.76],
  zoom: 12
});

const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // optional – lets the plugin bind to the map automatically
  placeholder: 'Search places…',
  marker: true,                // add a marker at the result location
  collapsed: false            // show the input box expanded by default
});

// Add the UI control to the map
map.addControl(geocoder);
``` |
| **Features** | * Autocomplete with Mapbox’s **Geocoding API** (global coverage, POI, address, reverse‑geocode). <br>* Built‑in UI (search box, clear button, loading spinner). <br>* Optional marker, fly‑to animation, language & proximity options. <br>* Supports **forward** and **reverse** geocoding out‑of‑the‑box. |
| **Pros** | • Tight integration – the plugin knows how to call the Mapbox API with the same token you already have. <br>• Very low‑effort – just drop a control on the map. <br>• Rich result types (address, place, country, postcode, etc.). |
| **Cons** | • **Requires a Mapbox access token** (and you pay per 1 000 requests after the free tier). <br>• Tied to Mapbox’s **terms of service** (must show Mapbox attribution, cannot use for prohibited content). <br>• If you ever want to move off Mapbox (e.g., to MapLibre), you’ll need to replace this component. |
| **Gotchas** | • The plugin uses **fetch** to call `https://api.mapbox.com/geocoding/v5/...`. If you are behind a CSP, allow `api.mapbox.com`. <br>• The default UI adds a `mapboxgl-ctrl-geocoder` CSS class; if you rename the Mapbox namespace (e.g., after a migration) you must also adjust any custom CSS. <br>• The geocoder respects the map’s `language` and `proximity` options only if you pass them explicitly (`geocoder.setLanguage('es')`, `geocoder.setProximity({lng:…, lat:…})`). |
| **When to use** | • You already have a Mapbox token and are happy paying for Mapbox Geocoding. <br>• You need the fastest, most feature‑complete search UI with minimal code. |

---

## 2️⃣ Open‑Source / Self‑Hosted Alternatives (still usable with Mapbox GL JS v2)

These libraries **do not require a Mapbox token**. They call an external (often free) geocoding service, or you can self‑host the service yourself. The UI component is the same or very similar to the Mapbox plugin, so you can swap it in with only a few lines of code.

| # | Library | Service it talks to | Install / CDN | Example integration | Pros | Cons |
|---|---------|---------------------|---------------|---------------------|------|------|
| **2.1** | **MapLibre GL Geocoder** (fork of Mapbox GL Geocoder) | Any HTTP‑compatible geocoder (Mapbox, OpenStreetMap Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler, etc.) – you configure the endpoint yourself. | `npm install @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder` <br>or CDN: `https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder@latest/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.min.js` | ```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl'; // you can keep using mapbox-gl v2
import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … */ });

const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  // Choose any public endpoint – here we use Nominatim (no API key needed)
  url: 'https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search',
  // Nominatim expects `format=json` and `addressdetails=1`
  queryParams: { format: 'json', addressdetails: 1 },
  // Optional: add a marker when a result is selected
  marker: true,
  // Optional: limit results per request (default 5)
  limit: 5,
  // Optional: set a placeholder text
  placeholder: 'Search OSM…'
});

map.addControl(geocoder);
``` | • **No Mapbox token** required. <br>• Works with any geocoder that returns GeoJSON‑compatible results (you can even point it at a private, self‑hosted service). <br>• Same UI as the Mapbox plugin, so you can keep your CSS. | • You must **pick / host** a geocoder yourself. <br>• Some services (e.g., public Nominatim) have strict usage limits; you may need to self‑host for production. |
| **2.2** | **OpenCage Geocoder UI** (thin wrapper) | OpenCage Geocoding API (requires a free API key, generous free tier). | `npm install @opencage/geocoder` (or just use fetch) + custom UI (no ready‑made control). | ```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … */ });

// Simple HTML input
const input = document.createElement('input');
input.type = 'search';
input.placeholder = 'Search…';
input.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;top:10px;left:10px;width:250px;z-index:1;';
document.body.appendChild(input);

input.addEventListener('keydown', async e => {
  if (e.key !== 'Enter') return;
  const q = encodeURIComponent(input.value);
  const key = '<YOUR_OPENCAGE_KEY>'; // free tier 2 500 req/day
  const resp = await fetch(`https://api.opencagedata.com/geocode/v1/json?q=${q}&key=${key}&limit=5&no_annotations=1`);
  const data = await resp.json();
  if (!data.results.length) return;
  const { lat, lng } = data.results[0].geometry;
  map.flyTo({ center: [lng, lat], zoom: 14 });
});
``` | • Very generous free tier (2 500 requests/day). <br>• Global coverage, good address quality. | • No ready‑made UI component – you have to build the dropdown yourself (or pair with a UI library). |
| **2.3** | **Photon UI** (via `leaflet-geosearch` or custom) | Photon (open‑source geocoder built on OpenStreetMap data, hosted at `https://photon.komoot.io`). | CDN: `https://unpkg.com/leaflet-geosearch@latest/dist/bundle.min.js` (works with any map library). | ```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import { GeoSearchControl, OpenStreetMapProvider } from 'leaflet-geosearch';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … */ });

// Leaflet‑Geosearch expects a Leaflet map, but you can reuse its UI component.
// Instead we create a tiny wrapper that forwards the result to Mapbox GL.
const provider = new OpenStreetMapProvider({
  // optional custom endpoint: 'https://photon.komoot.io/api/'
});

const searchControl = new GeoSearchControl({
  provider,
  style: 'bar', // minimal UI
  showMarker: true,
  retainZoomLevel: false,
  animateZoom: true,
  keepResult: true,
  // custom callback when a result is selected
  onResult: result => {
    const [lng, lat] = result.location;
    map.flyTo({ center: [lng, lat], zoom: 14 });
  }
});

// Append the control’s DOM element to the map container
document.getElementById('map').appendChild(searchControl.getContainer());
``` | • Free public endpoint (`photon.komoot.io`). <br>• Simple JSON response, easy to adapt. | • Not a native Mapbox‑GL plugin – you need a tiny wrapper to move the map. <br>• Public endpoint has rate limits; self‑host Photon for production. |
| **2.4** | **Algolia Places** (deprecated but still functional) | Algolia’s hosted place index (free tier, limited to 1 000 requests/day). | CDN: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/places.js@1.19.0` | ```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import places from 'places.js';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … */ });

const searchInput = document.createElement('input');
searchInput.id = 'address-search';
searchInput.type = 'search';
searchInput.placeholder = 'Search places…';
searchInput.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;top:10px;left:10px;width:250px;z-index:1;';
document.body.appendChild(searchInput);

const placesAutocomplete = places({
  appId: '<YOUR_ALGOLIA_APP_ID>',
  apiKey: '<YOUR_ALGOLIA_SEARCH_ONLY_API_KEY>',
  container: searchInput
});

placesAutocomplete.on('change', e => {
  const { latlng } = e.suggestion; // { lat:…, lng:… }
  map.fly
